A friend of mine here at work did the port a week or so ago and I've
been banging on it to check for errors and it seems pretty stable.

It's not Mac like at all - just what you see when you play on a unix
terminal. Also, because of the way the Mac works, theres a few more
data files that have to be loaded in at run time (you'll see the "You
hear the sound of heavy machinery..." as it reads them in). Also, just
as in the unix version, you have to restart the game every time you
die - a major annoyance cause it takes so long to start.

It takes up 2 floppies (500k for the application alone). If anyone is
interested, send me some e-mail and I'll see what I can do to get it
out. If there'e enough response I'll post it to comp.binaries.mac.
(which also means that I'll wait to see what kind of response I'll get
before sending it to anyone). If you really, really want it and can't
wait a few weeks for it to show up in comp.binaries.mac send me a
stamped, self-addressed envelope with 2 800k floppies and I'll send
them right back to you, with the hack files of course.
